Why the original code was wrong (brief):
- LAT requires dot-products mod 2: u = parity(a & x), v = parity(b & S(x)).
- Your code multiplies bits by a and b and treats b*fx as a whole value, which is incorrect.

Immediate fix (copy-paste-ready Java):
public final class Project_4 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // 3->3 S-box: S(0..7)
        int[] sbox = {0x6, 0x5, 0x1, 0x0, 0x3, 0x2, 0x7, 0x4};

        int[][] nlat = normalizedLat(sbox);

        // Print in the exact comma-separated format you provided
        for (int i = 0; i < nlat.length; i++) {
            StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
            for (int j = 0; j < nlat[i].length; j++) {
                if (j > 0) sb.append(", ");
                sb.append(nlat[i][j]);
            }
            System.out.println(sb.toString());
        }
    }

    // Compute normalized LAT: (# of x with <a,x> == <b,S(x)>) - 4
    private static int[][] normalizedLat(int[] sbox) {
        int n = sbox.length;   // 8
        int half = n / 2;      // 4
        int[][] table = new int[n][n];
        for (int a = 0; a < n; a++) {
            for (int b = 0; b < n; b++) {
                int countZero = 0;
                for (int x = 0; x < n; x++) {
                    int u = parity(a & x);        // <a, x>
                    int v = parity(b & sbox[x]);  // <b, S(x)>
                    if ((u ^ v) == 0) countZero++;
                }
                table[a][b] = countZero - half;   // normalize
            }
        }
        return table;
    }

    // Parity of bits (even->0, odd->1)
    private static int parity(int x) {
        return Integer.bitCount(x) & 1;
    }
}

Step-by-step implementation guide:
1) Keep S-box as int[] of size 8 with values 0..7 (already provided).
2) Add parity(int) using Integer.bitCount(x) & 1.
3) For each masks a,b in 0..7, iterate x in 0..7:
   - u = parity(a & x)
   - v = parity(b & sbox[x])
   - If (u ^ v) == 0, increment countZero.
4) Normalize each cell with countZero - 4.
5) Print rows as comma-separated values to match the expected output format.

