Permissions and capabilities
- Minimum: users must be able to create/edit their own Artiste posts. If your CPT uses default post caps, roles like Author can edit posts; Subscribers cannot by default. Options:
  - Simplest: keep this form owner-restricted and rely on post_author checks (as in the code). This lets even Subscribers manage their own Artiste via the custom form without granting backend caps, because insertion is performed by your code. Avoid exposing generic endpoints.
  - Hardened: register the CPT with custom capabilities (capability_type => ['artiste','artistes'], map_meta_cap => true) and grant those to the Ultimate Member roles allowed to manage the Artiste.

Security considerations
- Nonces: Required for create/update and delete (implemented).
- Authorization: Enforce ownership (post_author === current user) and UM role check (implemented).
- File uploads: Validate mime types and size; use media_handle_upload (implemented). Consider additional server-side image scanning if needed.
- Sanitization/escaping: Sanitize incoming fields and escape on output (implemented). Replace sanitize callbacks as appropriate for your fields.
- Status workflow: Use draft/pending and review before publishing.

Where to place the code
- Preferred: as a small custom plugin (as shown) to keep changes versionable and independent of the theme.
- Alternative: functions.php works, but avoid for long-term maintainability.

Displaying custom fields in the tab
- Edit mode: fields are rendered as inputs for the owner (umart_render_edit_ui). Replace the IDs in umart_config()['fields'] with your Meta Box field IDs. Values are read/written via get_post_meta/update_post_meta.
- Read-only mode: viewers see a formatted list (umart_render_readonly_ui).

Integration with Meta Box
- This example interacts with Meta Box fields at the storage level (post meta). If your fields are saved under different keys or use complex field types (group/cloneable), adapt the save/load parts accordingly.

Potential limitations with free versions
- Ultimate Member (free):
  - No built-in post management UI; we create a custom tab and forms manually.
  - Advanced access controls or workflow features may require UM extensions.
- Meta Box (free core):
  - Frontend form generation helpers (e.g., MB Frontend Submission) are paid; the example hand-builds the form and saves meta directly.
  - Complex field types (groups, clones, repeaters) require additional handling in custom code or paid extensions.
- Media handling: no fine-grained upload restrictions per role without extra code or plugins.
- Moderation: no built-in review queue in UM; rely on WordPress post statuses and admin screens.

Alternative approaches and best practices
- Use Meta Box extensions: If you own MB Frontend Submission, you can render and process the Artiste form with a shortcode on the UM tab content, reducing custom code. Pair with MB Custom Post Types/Taxonomies for GUI management.
- Use a dedicated frontend post plugin: Plugins like WP User Frontend, ACF Frontend, or Toolset Forms can provide full frontend CRUD and can be embedded inside a UM profile tab via shortcode or template hooks.
- Custom capabilities + UM role mapping: Define bespoke artiste caps and map them to UM roles for clearer permissioning and future-proofing.
- Workflow: keep create/update as draft or pending; notify admins on submission; publish after review. Add email hooks on save_post_artiste.
- UX: separate “View” and “Edit” sub-states, add success/error notices, and confirm destructive actions.
- Performance: cache read-only output with transients; clear on post save.
- i18n: wrap strings in translation functions if you need localization.

Information needed from you to finalize the code
- Your exact CPT slug (if not "artiste") and whether it’s already registered elsewhere.
- The precise Meta Box field IDs (and types) you want to display/edit.
- Desired post statuses on create/update (draft, pending, publish).
- Which UM roles should be allowed to manage Artiste.
- Whether you want to enforce one-per-user, and how to treat deletions (trash vs force).
- Any additional fields (taxonomies, repeaters, groups) or validations you need.
- Any custom URL structure or listing page where Artiste posts are displayed.

function source_panel_main()
% SOURCE_PANEL_MAIN
% 2-D constant-strength source panel method for potential flow around a
% closed body. Reads panel points from a text file, prompts for flow
% conditions, computes pressure coefficients and lift coefficient, and
% compares with analytical results when available. Also performs a simple
% panel refinement study for accuracy assessment (geometry permitting).
%
% INPUT FILE FORMAT (text):
%   Each row: x  y
%   The list should define a closed contour in either clockwise or
%   counter-clockwise order. The last point need not repeat the first; the
%   code will close the loop automatically.
%
% NOTE:
%   - Pure source-panel method (without a vortex sheet) yields zero net
%     circulation and thus zero lift for symmetric bodies at small AoA.
%     For analytical comparisons of Cp and Cl, this script supports:
%       * Circle in uniform flow (zero AoA): analytic Cp available.
%       * Joukowski airfoil-like comparisons are not included here.
%     The script still reports the numerically integrated lift and a
%     Kutta–Joukowski estimate based on computed circulation (expected near
%     zero for source-only formulation).
%
% Robust I/O and error handling are included.

  clc; close all; clearvars -except varargin;
  fprintf('2-D Source Panel Method (Constant-Strength)\n');

  %--------------------------- Read geometry -----------------------------%
  geomFile = input('Enter path to panel points file (e.g., airfoil.txt): ', 's');
  if isempty(geomFile)
      error('No geometry file provided.');
  end
  if ~isfile(geomFile)
      error('Geometry file not found: %s', geomFile);
  end
  P = readPanelPoints(geomFile); % Nx2 array
  % Ensure closed loop
  if norm(P(end,:) - P(1,:)) > 1e-12
      P = [P; P(1,:)];
  end

  %----------------------- Prompt flow conditions -----------------------%
  Uinf = inputWithDefault('Enter free-stream speed Uinf [m/s] (default 1): ', 1.0, @isPositive);
  alpha_deg = inputWithDefault('Enter angle of attack alpha [deg] (default 0): ', 0.0, @isnumeric);
  rho = inputWithDefault('Enter density rho [kg/m^3] (default 1.225): ', 1.225, @isPositive);
  alpha = deg2rad(alpha_deg);
  U = [Uinf*cos(alpha), Uinf*sin(alpha)];

  %--------------------------- Build panels -----------------------------%
  panels = buildPanels(P);
  N = numel(panels);
  fprintf('Loaded %d panels.\n', N);

  %--------------------- Solve source strengths -------------------------%
  [A, RHS] = influenceMatrix(panels, U);
  % Enforce zero net source (impermeability on closed body implies this)
  % Add one equation: sum(lambda_i * Li) = 0 with a small Tikhonov stabilization
  Li = [panels.L]';
  Aaug = [A,          zeros(N,1); 
          Li.',       0          ];
  RHSaug = [RHS; 0];

  lambda_aug = Aaug \ RHSaug; % [lambda; auxiliary]
  lambda = lambda_aug(1:N);

  %------------------- Compute surface velocities/Cp --------------------%
  [Vt, Vmag, Cp] = surfaceVelocitiesAndCp(panels, lambda, U, Uinf);

  %------------------ Estimate circulation and Cl -----------------------%
  % For source-only method, circulation is approximately zero. We can
  % approximate gamma_tangential along surface via panel-averaged tangential
  % velocity deficit. Then integrate around body to estimate Gamma.
  Gamma = trapezoidSum([panels.s], Vt); % crude estimate of circulation
  Cl_KJ = 2*Gamma/(Uinf*characteristicChord(panels)); % Kutta–Joukowski based non-dimensionalization using c

  % Pressure-based lift coefficient using surface pressure integration
  [Cl_pressure, Lprime] = pressureLiftCoefficient(panels, Cp, rho, Uinf);

  %---------------- Analytical comparisons where available --------------%
  analytic = struct('hasAnalytic', false);
  [isCircle, R, center] = detectCircle(P);
  if isCircle && abs(alpha_deg) < 1e-8
      analytic.hasAnalytic = true;
      analytic.type = 'Circle, uniform flow, zero AoA';
      analytic.Cp_fun = @(theta) 1 - 4*(sin(theta)).^2; % Cp(theta)
      analytic.Cl = 0.0;
      % Map each panel control point to polar angle
      xc = arrayfun(@(p) p.xc, panels)';
      yc = arrayfun(@(p) p.yc, panels)';
      theta = atan2(yc - center(2), xc - center(1));
      Cp_analytic = analytic.Cp_fun(theta);
      Cl_analytic = analytic.Cl;
  else
      Cp_analytic = nan(size(Cp));
      Cl_analytic = nan;
  end

  %--------------------- Accuracy / refinement study --------------------%
  doStudy = inputWithDefault('Run panel refinement study? 1=yes, 0=no (default 0): ', 0, @(x) x==0 || x==1);
  study = [];
  if doStudy
      % Construct rediscretizations by arc-length to different Npan values
      targetN = inputWithDefault('Enter vector of panel counts, e.g., [40 80 160]: ', [N, 2*N], @(x) isnumeric(x) && all(x>4));
      study = refinementStudy(P, targetN, U, Uinf, rho, alpha_deg, analytic);
  end

  %------------------------------ Outputs -------------------------------%
  fprintf('\n=== Results ================================\n');
  fprintf('Panels: %d\n', N);
  fprintf('Uinf: %.4g m/s, alpha: %.4g deg, rho: %.4g kg/m^3\n', Uinf, alpha_deg, rho);

  if analytic.hasAnalytic
      % Compute error metrics
      mask = isfinite(Cp_analytic);
      Cp_err_rms = sqrt(mean((Cp(mask)-Cp_analytic(mask)).^2));
      fprintf('Analytical case detected: %s\n', analytic.type);
      fprintf('RMS(Cp error): %.3e\n', Cp_err_rms);
      fprintf('Cl (pressure-integration): %.6f, analytic: %.6f\n', Cl_pressure, Cl_analytic);
  else
      fprintf('No analytic Cp/Cl available for this geometry/AoA.\n');
  end

  fprintf('Estimated circulation Gamma: %.6e [m^2/s]\n', Gamma);
  fprintf('Cl (Kutta–Joukowski, from Gamma): %.6f\n', Cl_KJ);
  fprintf('Cl (pressure integration): %.6f\n', Cl_pressure);
  fprintf('L'' per span (pressure integration): %.6f N/m\n', Lprime);

  % Plots
  figure('Name','Geometry and Cp');
  subplot(1,2,1); hold on; axis equal; grid on; box on;
  plot(P(:,1), P(:,2), 'k.-'); title('Geometry'); xlabel('x'); ylabel('y');
  subplot(1,2,2); hold on; grid on; box on;
  s_panel = cumulativeArcLength(panels);
  plot(s_panel, Cp, 'b.-', 'DisplayName','Computed Cp');
  if analytic.hasAnalytic
      plot(s_panel, Cp_analytic, 'r--', 'DisplayName','Analytic Cp');
      legend('Location','best');
  end
  set(gca,'YDir','reverse'); ylabel('Cp'); xlabel('s (along surface)'); title('Pressure Coefficient');

  if ~isempty(study)
      figure('Name','Refinement Study'); hold on; grid on; box on;
      plot([study.N]', [study.Cl_pressure]', 'o-', 'DisplayName','Cl (pressure)');
      plot([study.N]', [study.Cl_KJ]', 's-', 'DisplayName','Cl (KJ)');
      ylabel('Cl'); xlabel('Number of panels'); legend('Location','best'); title('Refinement of Cl');
      if isfield(study, 'Cp_rms') && any(isfinite([study.Cp_rms]))
          figure('Name','Cp RMS Error vs N'); hold on; grid on; box on;
          plot([study.N]', [study.Cp_rms]', 'o-'); xlabel('Number of panels'); ylabel('RMS Cp error'); title('Accuracy vs Discretization');
      end
  end

  fprintf('Done.\n');
end

%============================== Helpers ==================================%
function P = readPanelPoints(fname)
  data = readmatrix(fname);
  if isempty(data) || size(data,2) < 2
      error('Geometry file must contain at least two columns [x y].');
  end
  P = data(:,1:2);
  % Remove NaNs or duplicate trailing points
  P = P(all(isfinite(P),2),:);
  % Remove consecutive duplicates
  keep = [true; any(diff(P,1,1)~=0,2)];
  P = P(keep,:);
  if size(P,1) < 3
      error('At least 3 unique points required to form a closed contour.');
  end
end

function ok = isPositive(x)
  ok = isnumeric(x) && isscalar(x) && x > 0;
end

function val = inputWithDefault(prompt, defaultVal, validator)
  if nargin < 3 || isempty(validator)
      validator = @(x) true;
  end
  while true
      s = input(prompt, 's');
      if isempty(s)
          val = defaultVal; return;
      end
      try
          v = evalin('base', s); %#ok<EVLDIR>
      catch
          v = str2double(s);
      end
      if isempty(v) || any(~isfinite(v), 'all')
          fprintf('Invalid input. Try again.\n'); continue;
      end
      if validator(v)
          val = v; return;
      else
          fprintf('Input failed validation. Try again.\n');
      end
  end
end

function panels = buildPanels(P)
  % Build straight panels with geometry and collocation points
  N = size(P,1)-1;
  panels = repmat(struct('x1',0,'y1',0,'x2',0,'y2',0,'xc',0,'yc',0, ...
                         'tx',0,'ty',0,'nx',0,'ny',0,'L',0,'s',0), N, 1);
  s_acc = 0;
  for i = 1:N
      x1 = P(i,1); y1 = P(i,2);
      x2 = P(i+1,1); y2 = P(i+1,2);
      dx = x2 - x1; dy = y2 - y1; L = hypot(dx,dy);
      if L < 1e-12
          error('Degenerate panel of near-zero length at index %d.', i);
      end
      tx = dx/L; ty = dy/L;           % tangential unit vector
      nx =  ty;  ny = -tx;            % outward normal (rotate +90 deg)
      xc = 0.5*(x1+x2); yc = 0.5*(y1+y2);
      s_acc = s_acc + L;
      panels(i) = struct('x1',x1,'y1',y1,'x2',x2,'y2',y2,'xc',xc,'yc',yc, ...
                         'tx',tx,'ty',ty,'nx',nx,'ny',ny,'L',L,'s',s_acc);
  end
end

function [A, RHS] = influenceMatrix(panels, U)
  % A_ij = normal velocity at control point i induced by unit source on panel j
  % RHS_i enforces no-penetration: (U dot n_i) + sum_j (lambda_j * a_ij) = 0
  N = numel(panels);
  A = zeros(N,N);
  RHS = zeros(N,1);
  for i = 1:N
      ni = [panels(i).nx, panels(i).ny];
      RHS(i) = -dot(U, ni);
      for j = 1:N
          A(i,j) = sourcePanelNormalInfluence(panels(i), panels(j));
      end
  end
end

function a = sourcePanelNormalInfluence(pi, pj)
  % Normal component of velocity induced at control point of panel i by
  % a constant-strength source (strength = 1) distributed along panel j.
  % Uses standard analytical expressions via local coordinates.
  % Reference: Katz & Plotkin or standard panel method notes.
  x = pi.xc; y = pi.yc;
  % Transform control point to panel-j local frame
  xj1 = pj.x1; yj1 = pj.y1; tx = pj.tx; ty = pj.ty; nx = pj.nx; ny = pj.ny; L = pj.L;
  % Vector from j-panel start to control point
  dx = x - xj1; dy = y - yj1;
  xloc =  dx*tx + dy*ty; % along panel
  yloc =  dx*nx + dy*ny; % normal to panel (positive outward)

  % Avoid singularities with small epsilon
  eps = 1e-12;
  yloc = max(min(yloc, 1/eps), -1/eps); % keep finite

  % Define endpoints in local x
  x2 = xloc - L; x1 = xloc;
  r1 = hypot(x1, yloc) + eps;
  r2 = hypot(x2, yloc) + eps;

  % Influence formulas for unit source panel
  % Normal velocity component Vn at (xloc, yloc):
  % Vn = (1/(2*pi)) * (atan2(x2*yloc, r2^2) - atan2(x1*yloc, r1^2))
  % Derivation uses potential of a line source; normal is local y.
  a = (1/(2*pi)) * (atan2(x2*yloc, r2^2) - atan2(x1*yloc, r1^2));

  % Self-influence correction (i==j) handled naturally; numerical stability
  % is improved by eps in radii. For strictly on-surface collocation, this
  % expression yields finite principal value.
end

function [Vt, Vmag, Cp] = surfaceVelocitiesAndCp(panels, lambda, U, Uinf)
  N = numel(panels);
  Vt = zeros(N,1);
  Vmag = zeros(N,1);
  for i = 1:N
      % Induced velocity at control point i from all source panels
      Ui = U; % start with freestream
      for j = 1:N
          uij = sourcePanelVelocityAtPoint(panels(i).xc, panels(i).yc, panels(j));
          Ui = Ui + lambda(j) * uij;
      end
      % Tangential/normal components
      ti = [panels(i).tx, panels(i).ty];
      Vt(i) = dot(Ui, ti);
      Vmag(i) = norm(Ui);
  end
  Cp = 1 - (Vmag./Uinf).^2;
end

function u = sourcePanelVelocityAtPoint(x, y, pj)
  % Velocity vector induced by unit source strength on panel pj at (x,y)
  % Using standard closed-form expressions in local coordinates, then rotate
  % back to global.
  xj1 = pj.x1; yj1 = pj.y1; tx = pj.tx; ty = pj.ty; nx = pj.nx; ny = pj.ny; L = pj.L;
  dx = x - xj1; dy = y - yj1;
  xloc =  dx*tx + dy*ty;
  yloc =  dx*nx + dy*ny;

  eps = 1e-12;
  x1 = xloc; x2 = xloc - L;
  r1 = hypot(x1, yloc) + eps; r2 = hypot(x2, yloc) + eps;

  % Local components from unit source panel (see Katz & Plotkin):
  % u_xloc = (1/(2*pi)) * (ln(r2/r1))
  % u_yloc = (1/(2*pi)) * (atan2(x2*yloc, r2^2) - atan2(x1*yloc, r1^2))
  ux_loc = (1/(2*pi)) * log(r2./r1);
  uy_loc = (1/(2*pi)) * (atan2(x2*yloc, r2.^2) - atan2(x1*yloc, r1.^2));

  % Rotate back to global frame
  u = [ux_loc*tx + uy_loc*nx, ux_loc*ty + uy_loc*ny];
end

function s = cumulativeArcLength(panels)
  s = [panels.s]';
  s = s - s(1);
end

function c = characteristicChord(panels)
  % Use projected x-extent as a chord-like length scale
  xs = [panels.x1, panels.x2]; xs = xs(:);
  c = max(xs) - min(xs);
  if c <= 0
      c = sum([panels.L]); % fallback: perimeter length
  end
end

function S = trapezoidSum(s_along, f)
  % Approximate line integral via trapezoidal rule along panel arc length
  % s_along should be panel cumulative positions; if not provided, use panel
  % lengths as equal steps.
  if numel(s_along) ~= numel(f)
      s_along = (1:numel(f))';
  end
  [s_along, idx] = sort(s_along(:)); f = f(idx);
  ds = diff(s_along);
  S = sum(0.5*(f(1:end-1) + f(2:end)).*ds);
end

function [isCirc, R, c] = detectCircle(P)
  % Simple circle fit via linear least squares (Kasa method)
  x = P(:,1); y = P(:,2);
  A = [2*x, 2*y, ones(size(x))];
  b = x.^2 + y.^2;
  if rank(A) < 3
      isCirc = false; R = NaN; c = [NaN, NaN]; return;
  end
  sol = A\b;
  cx = sol(1); cy = sol(2); c = [cx, cy];
  R = sqrt(sol(3) + cx^2 + cy^2);
  % Heuristic: if residuals are small compared to R, deem circle
  r = hypot(x-cx, y-cy);
  res = std(r - mean(r));
  isCirc = isfinite(R) && R>0 && res < 1e-3*R;
end

function [Cl_pressure, Lprime] = pressureLiftCoefficient(panels, Cp, rho, Uinf)
  % Integrate pressure over the surface to get lift per unit span, then Cl
  % p - p_inf = 0.5*rho*Uinf^2 * Cp
  q = 0.5*rho*Uinf^2;
  N = numel(panels);
  Fy = 0;
  for i = 1:N
      % Pressure acts inward along normal; outward normal defined in panels
      % Lift positive upward (y-direction): contribution = -p * (ny) * L
      p = q * Cp(i);
      Fy = Fy - p * panels(i).ny * panels(i).L;
  end
  Lprime = Fy; % N/m
  c = characteristicChord(panels);
  Cl_pressure = Lprime / (0.5*rho*Uinf^2 * c);
end

function study = refinementStudy(P, targetN, U, Uinf, rho, alpha_deg, analytic)
  targetN = targetN(:)';
  study = struct('N', {}, 'Cl_KJ', {}, 'Cl_pressure', {}, 'Cp_rms', {});
  for k = 1:numel(targetN)
      Nk = max(4, round(targetN(k)));
      Pk = rediscretizeByArc(P, Nk);
      panels = buildPanels(Pk);
      [A, RHS] = influenceMatrix(panels, U);
      Li = [panels.L]';
      Aaug = [A, zeros(Nk,1); Li.', 0]; RHSaug = [RHS; 0];
      lambda = (Aaug \ RHSaug); lambda = lambda(1:Nk);
      [Vt, Vmag, Cp] = surfaceVelocitiesAndCp(panels, lambda, U, Uinf); %#ok<ASGLU>
      Gamma = trapezoidSum([panels.s], Vt);
      Cl_KJ = 2*Gamma/(Uinf*characteristicChord(panels));
      [Cl_p, ~] = pressureLiftCoefficient(panels, Cp, rho, Uinf);
      Cp_rms = NaN;
      if analytic.hasAnalytic
          [isCircle, ~, center] = detectCircle([ [panels.x1]', [panels.y1]'; panels(1).x1, panels(1).y1 ]); %#ok<NASGU>
          xc = arrayfun(@(p) p.xc, panels)';
          yc = arrayfun(@(p) p.yc, panels)';
          theta = atan2(yc - center(2), xc - center(1));
          Cp_analytic = analytic.Cp_fun(theta);
          mask = isfinite(Cp_analytic);
          Cp_rms = sqrt(mean((Cp(mask)-Cp_analytic(mask)).^2));
      end
      study(k) = struct('N', Nk, 'Cl_KJ', Cl_KJ, 'Cl_pressure', Cl_p, 'Cp_rms', Cp_rms);
  end
end

function Pk = rediscretizeByArc(P, N)
  % Rediscretize the closed polyline P into N panels (N+1 points, closed)
  if norm(P(end,:) - P(1,:)) > 1e-12
      P = [P; P(1,:)];
  end
  seg = diff(P,1,1);
  Lseg = hypot(seg(:,1), seg(:,2));
  s = [0; cumsum(Lseg)];
  Ltot = s(end);
  if Ltot <= 0
      error('Zero total length in geometry.');
  end
  s_new = linspace(0, Ltot, N+1).';
  Pk = interp1(s, P, s_new, 'linear');
  if any(any(~isfinite(Pk)))
      error('Rediscretization produced invalid points.');
  end
end

Below is a complete, self-contained MATLAB implementation of a 2-D source panel method that: (a) reads panel points from a text file, (b) prompts the user for free-stream speed and angle of attack, (c) computes pressure coefficient distribution, (d) computes lift coefficient using Kutta–Joukowski (with optional analytical comparison for a circle or thin-airfoil theory), and (e) optionally checks accuracy by varying panel counts if multiple files are provided. Save as source_panel_main.m and run. A sample input format is documented in comments.

% ============================
% File: source_panel_main.m
% ============================
function source_panel_main()
    clc; close all;
    fprintf('2-D Source Panel Method (MATLAB)\n');
    fprintf('--------------------------------\n');

    % -- Input: panel coordinates file(s)
    % Expected file format (ASCII text):
    % Either:
    %   x1  y1
    %   x2  y2
    %   ...
    %   xN  yN
    % with last point equal to first point (closed). If not closed, code will close it.
    % You may also provide multiple files separated by commas to compare accuracy vs. panel counts.
    filestr = input('Enter path to panel point file (or multiple, comma-separated): ', 's');
    filelist = strtrim(strsplit(filestr, ','));

    % -- Flow conditions
    Uinf = input('Enter free-stream speed U_inf [m/s]: ');
    alpha_deg = input('Enter angle of attack alpha [deg]: ');
    alpha = deg2rad(alpha_deg);
    rho = input('Enter fluid density rho [kg/m^3] (default 1.225): ');
    if isempty(rho); rho = 1.225; end

    % -- Optional analytical comparison selection
    fprintf('\nAnalytical comparison options:\n');
    fprintf('  0: None (generic body)\n');
    fprintf('  1: Circle of radius R (source panel should approximate circle).\n');
    fprintf('  2: Thin-airfoil theory (flat plate) CL = 2*pi*alpha (alpha in radians).\n');
    compChoice = input('Select analytical comparison [0/1/2] (default 0): ');
    if isempty(compChoice); compChoice = 0; end
    R_circle = NaN;
    if compChoice == 1
        R_circle = input('Enter circle radius R [m] (for analytical CP on cylinder at small alpha): ');
    end

    results = struct('N', {}, 'CL', {}, 'CL_analytical', {}, 'CL_error', {}, 'filesrc', {});

    for f = 1:numel(filelist)
        filesrc = filelist{f};
        try
            P = read_panel_points(filesrc);
        catch ME
            warning('Failed to read %s: %s', filesrc, ME.message);
            continue;
        end

        % Discretize into panels
        panels = build_panels(P);
        N = numel(panels);
        fprintf('\n--- Solving for file: %s (N = %d panels) ---\n', filesrc, N);

        % Assemble and solve source strengths
        [A, RHS] = assemble_influence_matrix(panels, Uinf, alpha);
        sigma = A\RHS; % source strength per unit length on each panel

        % Compute tangential velocity and Cp on control points
        [Vt, Cp] = compute_tangential_velocity_and_cp(panels, sigma, Uinf, alpha);

        % Compute lift coefficient via Kutta–Joukowski (circulation from tangential velocity)
        [CL, Gamma] = compute_cl_kj(panels, Vt, Uinf);

        % Optional analytical comparison
        CL_analytical = NaN; CL_error = NaN;
        if compChoice == 2
            CL_analytical = 2*pi*alpha; % thin-airfoil theory
            CL_error = CL - CL_analytical;
        elseif compChoice == 1
            % For a cylinder at small alpha, net lift per unit span L' = rho*Uinf*Gamma;
            % Theoretical circulation ~ 2*pi*Uinf*R^2*(dtheta/ds?) — exact match requires vortex sheet.
            % Source-only panels cannot generate lift on a symmetric closed body by themselves.
            % We report that analytical CL for cylinder with no circulation is 0.
            CL_analytical = 0;
            CL_error = CL - CL_analytical;
        end

        % Report
        fprintf('Lift coefficient (from Kutta–Joukowski): CL = %.6f\n', CL);
        if ~isnan(CL_analytical)
            fprintf('Analytical CL = %.6f ; Error = %.6f\n', CL_analytical, CL_error);
        end

        % Plot Cp distribution
        s = cumsum([0, arrayfun(@(p) p.S, panels(1:end-1))]);
        figure('Name', sprintf('Cp distribution - %s', filesrc));
        plot(s, Cp, 'o-'); grid on; xlabel('Panel arc length s'); ylabel('C_p');
        title(sprintf('Pressure coefficient distribution (N=%d)', N));

        % If analytical comparison for circle, plot approximate analytical Cp for cylinder w/out circulation
        if compChoice == 1 && ~isnan(R_circle)
            theta = atan2([panels.ctry]-0, [panels.ctrx]-0); % assuming centered near origin
            Cp_cyl = 1 - 4*(sin(theta - alpha)).^2; % potential flow around cylinder with no circulation
            hold on; plot(s, Cp_cyl, 'r--', 'DisplayName', 'Analytical (cylinder, no circ.)'); legend('show');
        elseif compChoice == 2
            % Thin-airfoil theory gives pressure jump proportional to 2*Uinf*alpha; Cp distribution analytical needs airfoil camber.
            % For generic geometries we just report CL comparison above.
        end

        % Save results
        results(end+1) = struct('N', N, 'CL', CL, 'CL_analytical', CL_analytical, ...
                                'CL_error', CL_error, 'filesrc', filesrc); %#ok<AGROW>

        % Print a small table of Cp at a few points
        kshow = unique(round(linspace(1, N, min(N, 10))));
        fprintf('\nIndex   s        Cp\n');
        for k = kshow
            fprintf('%4d  %8.4f  % .5f\n', k, s(k), Cp(k));
        end
    end

    % If multiple discretizations provided, report accuracy trend (CL convergence)
    if numel(results) > 1
        fprintf('\nConvergence summary (by panel count):\n');
        [~, ord] = sort([results.N]); results = results(ord);
        for r = 1:numel(results)
            if isnan(results(r).CL_analytical)
                fprintf('N=%4d : CL=%.6f\n', results(r).N, results(r).CL);
            else
                fprintf('N=%4d : CL=%.6f (Analytical=%.6f, Error=%.6f)\n', ...
                    results(r).N, results(r).CL, results(r).CL_analytical, results(r).CL_error);
            end
        end
        figure('Name', 'CL convergence');
        plot([results.N], [results.CL], 'o-'); grid on; xlabel('N panels'); ylabel('CL'); title('CL vs panel count');
        if any(~isnan([results.CL_analytical]))
            hold on; yline(results(end).CL_analytical, 'r--', 'Analytical'); legend('Numerical','Analytical');
        end
    end

    fprintf('\nDone.\n');
end

% ----------------------------
% Read panel points from text
% ----------------------------
function P = read_panel_points(filename)
    if ~isfile(filename)
        error('File not found: %s', filename);
    end
    data = readmatrix(filename);
    if size(data,2) < 2
        error('File must contain at least two columns [x y].');
    end
    x = data(:,1); y = data(:,2);
    if any(~isfinite(x)) || any(~isfinite(y))
        error('Non-finite values found in input.');
    end
    % Ensure closed polygon
    if x(1) ~= x(end) || y(1) ~= y(end)
        x(end+1) = x(1); y(end+1) = y(1);
    end
    P = [x y];
    % Ensure consistent clockwise orientation (optional)
    if polygon_area(P) > 0
        P = flipud(P);
    end
end

function A = polygon_area(P)
    x = P(:,1); y = P(:,2);
    A = 0.5*sum(x(1:end-1).*y(2:end) - x(2:end).*y(1:end-1));
end

% ----------------------------
% Build panels from points
% ----------------------------
function panels = build_panels(P)
    x = P(:,1); y = P(:,2);
    N = numel(x)-1; % last equals first
    panels = struct('xi', {}, 'yi', {}, 'xj', {}, 'yj', {}, 'S', {}, 'nx', {}, 'ny', {}, 'tx', {}, 'ty', {}, 'ctrx', {}, 'ctry', {}, 'beta', {});
    for i = 1:N
        xi = x(i); yi = y(i); xj = x(i+1); yj = y(i+1);
        S  = hypot(xj - xi, yj - yi);
        tx = (xj - xi)/S; ty = (yj - yi)/S;           % tangent unit
        nx =  ty; ny = -tx;                           % outward normal (for CW ordering)
        ctrx = 0.5*(xi + xj); ctry = 0.5*(yi + yj);
        beta = atan2(ty, tx);
        panels(i) = struct('xi',xi,'yi',yi,'xj',xj,'yj',yj,'S',S,'nx',nx,'ny',ny,'tx',tx,'ty',ty,'ctrx',ctrx,'ctry',ctry,'beta',beta); %#ok<AGROW>
    end
end

% ---------------------------------------------
% Influence coefficients for source panel method
% ---------------------------------------------
function [A, RHS] = assemble_influence_matrix(panels, Uinf, alpha)
    N = numel(panels);
    A = zeros(N, N);
    RHS = zeros(N, 1);

    % Normal-velocity boundary condition: V_n(total) = 0 at control points
    for i = 1:N
        for j = 1:N
            A(i,j) = normal_influence(panels(i), panels(j));
        end
        % RHS is negative of free-stream normal velocity at panel i control point
        Ux = Uinf*cos(alpha); Uy = Uinf*sin(alpha);
        RHS(i) = - (Ux*panels(i).nx + Uy*panels(i).ny);
    end

    % Enforce zero net source (impermeability for closed body): sum(sigma_j * S_j) = 0
    % Replace last equation with this global condition, and RHS=0
    A(end,:) = [arrayfun(@(p) p.S, panels)];
    RHS(end) = 0;
end

function a = normal_influence(pi, pj)
    % Returns integral over panel j of (n_i · velocity at i due to unit source strength on j)
    % Using analytical expressions for straight panels (Hess-Smith style)
    % Place local coordinates with panel j along x'-axis
    dx = pi.ctrx - pj.xi; dy = pi.ctry - pj.yi;
    cosb = pj.tx; sinb = pj.ty; % orientation of panel j
    xprime =  dx*cosb + dy*sinb;
    yprime = -dx*sinb + dy*cosb;
    % Endpoints in local frame
    x2 = pj.S; x1 = 0; y = yprime;

    % Avoid singularities
    eps = 1e-12;
    y = sign(y).*max(abs(y), eps);

    % Influence of unit-strength source per unit length on normal velocity at control point i
    % Refer to Cebeci & Cousteix / Katz & Plotkin formulas:
    def = atan2((x2 - xprime), y) - atan2((x1 - xprime), y);
    logterm = 0.5*log(((x2 - xprime)^2 + y^2)/((x1 - xprime)^2 + y^2));
    % Velocity components in local frame at control point due to panel j (unit sigma)
    u_local = (1/(2*pi)) * logterm;     % along panel
    v_local = (1/(2*pi)) * def;         % normal to panel (positive y')
    % Rotate to global
    ug =  u_local*cosb - v_local*sinb;
    vg =  u_local*sinb + v_local*cosb;
    % Project onto normal of panel i
    a = ug*pi.nx + vg*pi.ny;
end

% ------------------------------------------------------
% Tangential velocity and pressure coefficient on panels
% ------------------------------------------------------
function [Vt, Cp] = compute_tangential_velocity_and_cp(panels, sigma, Uinf, alpha)
    N = numel(panels);
    Vt = zeros(N,1);
    for i = 1:N
        % Contribution from all source panels to tangential component at control point i
        Vt_i = 0;
        for j = 1:N
            Vt_i = Vt_i + tangential_influence(panels(i), panels(j)) * sigma(j);
        end
        % Add free-stream tangential component
        Ux = Uinf*cos(alpha); Uy = Uinf*sin(alpha);
        Vt(i) = Vt_i + (Ux*panels(i).tx + Uy*panels(i).ty);
    end
    Cp = 1 - (Vt./Uinf).^2;
end

function t = tangential_influence(pi, pj)
    % Tangential velocity at control point i due to unit source on panel j
    dx = pi.ctrx - pj.xi; dy = pi.ctry - pj.yi;
    cosb = pj.tx; sinb = pj.ty;
    xprime =  dx*cosb + dy*sinb;
    yprime = -dx*sinb + dy*cosb;
    x2 = pj.S; x1 = 0; y = yprime;

    eps = 1e-12;
    y = sign(y).*max(abs(y), eps);

    def = atan2((x2 - xprime), y) - atan2((x1 - xprime), y);
    logterm = 0.5*log(((x2 - xprime)^2 + y^2)/((x1 - xprime)^2 + y^2));

    u_local = (1/(2*pi)) * logterm;     % along panel
    v_local = (1/(2*pi)) * def;         % normal to panel

    ug =  u_local*cosb - v_local*sinb;
    vg =  u_local*sinb + v_local*cosb;

    % Project onto tangent of panel i
    t = ug*pi.tx + vg*pi.ty;
end

% ---------------------------
% Lift via Kutta–Joukowski
% ---------------------------
function [CL, Gamma] = compute_cl_kj(panels, Vt, Uinf)
    % Estimate circulation by integrating tangential velocity along the body surface
    % Gamma = integral(Vt * ds) around body
    ds = [panels.S]';
    Gamma = sum(Vt .* ds);
    % Non-dimensional coefficient: CL = 2*Gamma / (Uinf * c_eff)
    % We estimate an effective chord as max(x) - min(x)
    xall = [panels.xi, panels.xj]; xall = xall(:);
    c_eff = max(xall) - min(xall);
    if c_eff <= 0
        c_eff = sum(ds); % fallback to perimeter to avoid divide-by-zero
    end
    CL = 2 * Gamma / (Uinf * c_eff);
end

Below is a complete, self-contained MATLAB script that implements a 2-D source panel method with optional vortex sheet to enable lift at nonzero angle of attack. It reads panel points from a text file, prompts for flow conditions, computes Cp and lift coefficient, allows convergence/accuracy study by varying panel counts, and compares results with analytical (circle/cylinder) or user-supplied experimental data if provided.

Instructions for input file:
- Text file should contain either:
  1) A single closed polygon with N points (x y per row; last point may repeat the first — the code will handle closure), or
  2) Multiple discretizations for an accuracy study separated by blank lines. Each block is treated as a separate geometry resolution.

Save this as run_source_panel_2D.m and run. Example call: run_source_panel_2D

% ======================= run_source_panel_2D.m =======================
function run_source_panel_2D()
  clc; close all;
  fprintf('2-D Source Panel Method (with optional vortex sheet)\n');
  fprintf('--------------------------------------------------\n');

  %--- Get geometry file ---
  geomFile = input('Enter path to panel points file (txt): ', 's');
  if ~isfile(geomFile)
    error('File not found: %s', geomFile);
  end

  %--- Load all blocks (for accuracy study) ---
  blocks = load_geometry_blocks(geomFile);
  if isempty(blocks)
    error('No valid geometry blocks found in file.');
  end

  %--- Flow conditions ---
  Uinf = input_with_default('Free-stream speed Uinf [m/s] (default 1): ', 1.0);
  alpha_deg = input_with_default('Angle of attack alpha [deg] (default 0): ', 0.0);
  rho = input_with_default('Density rho [kg/m^3] (default 1.225): ', 1.225);
  useVortex = input_with_default('Use vortex sheet for lift? 1=yes, 0=no (default 1): ', 1) ~= 0;

  %--- Optional reference for comparisons ---
  fprintf('\nOptional: Provide analytical/experimental references for comparison.\n');
  refType = lower(strtrim(input('Reference type: none/circle/custom (default none): ', 's')));
  if isempty(refType); refType = 'none'; end

  expCpFile = '';
  if strcmp(refType,'custom')
    expCpFile = input('Path to experimental/analytical Cp(x) file [x Cp], optional (Enter to skip): ', 's');
    if ~isempty(expCpFile) && ~isfile(expCpFile)
      warning('Cp reference file not found. Skipping Cp comparison.');
      expCpFile = '';
    end
  end

  %--- Process each block (accuracy/convergence study if multiple) ---
  nBlocks = numel(blocks);
  results = struct('N',[],'CL',[],'Gamma',[],'Lprime',[]);

  for b = 1:nBlocks
    xy = blocks{b};
    xy = ensure_closed_polygon(xy);

    % Build panels
    panels = build_panels(xy);

    % Solve source + optional vortex strength
    [sigma, gamma, Vt, Cp, Vinf, alpha] = solve_source_panel(panels, Uinf, deg2rad(alpha_deg), useVortex);

    % Forces and coefficients
    [Lprime, CL] = forces_from_panels(panels, rho, Vinf, Vt, gamma); % per unit span

    % Report
    fprintf('\nBlock %d: Npanels = %d\n', b, numel(panels));
    fprintf('  Circulation gamma = %.6g [m^2/s] (Kutta-Joukowski if gamma used)\n', gamma);
    fprintf('  Lift per unit span L'' = %.6g [N/m]\n', Lprime);
    fprintf('  Lift coefficient CL = %.6g\n', CL);

    % Save result
    results(b).N = numel(panels);
    results(b).CL = CL;
    results(b).Gamma = gamma;
    results(b).Lprime = Lprime;

    % Comparison: analytical/experimental
    if strcmp(refType,'circle')
      % Attempt to infer radius and center for best-fit circle (rough estimate)
      [xc,yc,R] = fit_circle(xy);
      U = Vinf; a = alpha;  %#ok<NASGU> (alpha used conceptually)
      % For potential flow around cylinder with circulation gamma:
      % Theoretical Kutta-Joukowski lift per span: L' = rho * U * Gamma
      Lprime_th = rho * U * gamma;
      CL_th = Lprime_th / (0.5*rho*U^2*(2*R)); % reference chord = diameter
      fprintf('  [Analytical circle] CL_theory (K-J) = %.6g (chord=2R)\n', CL_th);
    elseif strcmp(refType,'custom') && ~isempty(expCpFile)
      try
        ref = readmatrix(expCpFile);
        ref = ref(all(isfinite(ref),2),:);
        if size(ref,2) >= 2
          xref = ref(:,1); Cpref = ref(:,2);
          % Map our panel midpoints to x, then compute simple L2 error vs nearest neighbor
          xm = arrayfun(@(p) p.xc, panels).';
          Cpi = interp1(xref, Cpref, xm, 'linear', 'extrap');
          errCp = sqrt(mean((Cpi - Cp(:)).^2));
          fprintf('  Cp RMSE vs provided reference: %.4g\n', errCp);
        end
      catch ME
        warning('Could not read/compare Cp reference: %s', ME.message);
      end
    end

    % Plot Cp
    figure('Name',sprintf('Cp N=%d',numel(panels))); hold on; grid on;
    xm = arrayfun(@(p) p.xc, panels);
    plot(xm, Cp, '-o'); set(gca,'YDir','reverse');
    xlabel('x'); ylabel('C_p'); title(sprintf('Pressure Coefficient (N=%d)', numel(panels)));

  end

  % Accuracy/convergence assessment across blocks (if multiple)
  if nBlocks > 1
    Ns = [results.N]; CLs = [results.CL];
    figure('Name','Convergence CL'); plot(Ns, CLs, '-o'); grid on;
    xlabel('Number of panels'); ylabel('C_L'); title('Convergence of C_L with panel count');

    % Report simple relative change
    relChanges = abs(diff(CLs))./max(1e-12,abs(CLs(1:end-1)));
    for k=1:numel(relChanges)
      fprintf('Delta CL between N=%d and N=%d: %.3e\n', results(k).N, results(k+1).N, relChanges(k));
    end
  end

  fprintf('\nDone.\n');
end

% --------------------- Helper Functions ---------------------
function val = input_with_default(prompt, default)
  s = input(prompt, 's');
  if isempty(s)
    val = default;
  else
    val = str2double(s);
    if ~isfinite(val)
      warning('Invalid input. Using default %.6g.', default);
      val = default;
    end
  end
end

function blocks = load_geometry_blocks(fname)
  % Reads geometry points, possibly with blank-line-separated blocks.
  txt = fileread(fname);
  lines = regexp(txt,'\r?\n','split');
  blocks = {};
  cur = [];
  for i=1:numel(lines)
    line = strtrim(lines{i});
    if isempty(line)
      if ~isempty(cur)
        blocks{end+1} = cur; %#ok<AGROW>
        cur = [];
      end
      continue;
    end
    vals = sscanf(line,'%f');
    if numel(vals) >= 2
      cur = [cur; vals(1) vals(2)]; %#ok<AGROW>
    end
  end
  if ~isempty(cur)
    blocks{end+1} = cur;
  end

  % Basic validation
  ok = true(1,numel(blocks));
  for k=1:numel(blocks)
    if size(blocks{k},1) < 3 || size(blocks{k},2) < 2
      ok(k) = false;
    end
  end
  blocks = blocks(ok);
end

function xy = ensure_closed_polygon(xy)
  if norm(xy(1,:) - xy(end,:)) > 1e-12
    xy = [xy; xy(1,:)];
  end
end

function panels = build_panels(xy)
  % Build straight panels from successive points
  N = size(xy,1)-1;
  panels = repmat(struct('x1',0,'y1',0,'x2',0,'y2',0,'xc',0,'yc',0,'len',0,'theta',0,'nx',0,'ny',0,'tx',0,'ty',0), N,1);
  for i=1:N
    x1 = xy(i,1); y1 = xy(i,2);
    x2 = xy(i+1,1); y2 = xy(i+1,2);
    dx = x2 - x1; dy = y2 - y1;
    L = hypot(dx,dy);
    theta = atan2(dy,dx);
    tx = cos(theta); ty = sin(theta);
    nx =  sin(theta); ny = -cos(theta); % outward normal for CCW ordering
    xc = 0.5*(x1+x2); yc = 0.5*(y1+y2);
    panels(i).x1=x1; panels(i).y1=y1; panels(i).x2=x2; panels(i).y2=y2;
    panels(i).xc=xc; panels(i).yc=yc; panels(i).len=L; panels(i).theta=theta;
    panels(i).nx=nx; panels(i).ny=ny; panels(i).tx=tx; panels(i).ty=ty;
  end
end

function [sigma, gamma, Vt, Cp, Uinf, alpha] = solve_source_panel(panels, Uinf, alpha, useVortex)
  N = numel(panels);

  % Build influence matrices for source panels (normal velocity influence)
  A = zeros(N,N); RHS = zeros(N,1);

  % Freestream normal component at collocation points
  Ux = Uinf*cos(alpha); Uy = Uinf*sin(alpha);
  for i=1:N
    Ui_n = Ux*panels(i).nx + Uy*panels(i).ny;
    RHS(i) = -Ui_n;
  end

  % Source panel normal influence coefficients
  for i=1:N
    for j=1:N
      A(i,j) = panel_source_normal_influence(panels(i), panels(j));
    end
  end

  gamma = 0; % default no vortex
  if useVortex
    % Add a constant-strength vortex sheet gamma on all panels: its normal velocity is zero,
    % but tangential velocity changes and Kutta condition needed to solve gamma.
    % We enforce Kutta condition by requiring tangential velocity to be finite at trailing edge.
    % Here we add an additional unknown (gamma) and one equation: sum of tangential velocities at TE panels equal.

    % Extend system with gamma affecting normal velocity: for 2D, a uniform vortex sheet gives zero normal vel.
    % So normal system remains same; we need Kutta eqn via tangential velocities to determine gamma.

    % Solve sources first from normal boundary condition independent of gamma
    sigma = A \ RHS;

    % Now enforce Kutta via tangential velocity equality at ends: Vt(1)=Vt(N)
    % Compute Vt at each collocation as function of gamma
    % Vt = U_t + Vt_from_sources + Vt_from_gamma
    Ut = Ux*arrayfun(@(p) p.tx, panels).' + Uy*arrayfun(@(p) p.ty, panels).';
    Vt_src = zeros(N,1);
    for i=1:N
      s = 0;
      for j=1:N
        s = s + panel_source_tangential_influence(panels(i), panels(j))*sigma(j);
      end
      Vt_src(i) = s;
    end
    % Tangential influence from a uniform gamma over the body equals +gamma/2 (jump) on one side and -gamma/2 on the other.
    % At the surface we take mean, resulting in induced tangential velocity of gamma/2 with sign depending on convention.
    % We use Vt_gamma = +gamma/2 at all panels (convention absorbed in Kutta sign below).
    Vt_gamma_coeff = 0.5; % dVt/dgamma

    % Kutta condition: Vt(1) = -Vt(N) for sharp TE (common thin-airfoil convention)
    % Here adopt Vt(1) + Vt(N) = 0 to determine gamma.
    Vt1_wo = Ut(1) + Vt_src(1);
    VtN_wo = Ut(end) + Vt_src(end);
    gamma = -(Vt1_wo + VtN_wo) / (2*Vt_gamma_coeff);

  else
    % No vortex sheet: solve only sources
    sigma = A \ RHS;
  end

  % Compute tangential velocity distribution and Cp
  Ut = Ux*arrayfun(@(p) p.tx, panels).' + Uy*arrayfun(@(p) p.ty, panels).';
  Vt_src = zeros(N,1);
  for i=1:N
    s = 0;
    for j=1:N
      s = s + panel_source_tangential_influence(panels(i), panels(j))*sigma(j);
    end
    Vt_src(i) = s;
  end
  Vt = Ut + Vt_src + 0.5*gamma; % add gamma contribution
  Cp = 1 - (Vt./Uinf).^2;
end

function aij = panel_source_normal_influence(pi, pj)
  % Normal velocity at collocation of panel i due to unit-strength source panel j
  % Based on standard constant-strength source panel formulae.
  % Transform to panel j local coordinates and integrate analytically.
  xci = pi.xc; yci = pi.yc;
  x1 = pj.x1; y1 = pj.y1; x2 = pj.x2; y2 = pj.y2;
  dx = x2 - x1; dy = y2 - y1; L = pj.len; theta = pj.theta;

  % Rotate to local coordinates of panel j
  ct = cos(theta); st = sin(theta);
  xt =  ct*(xci - x1) + st*(yci - y1);
  yt = -st*(xci - x1) + ct*(yci - y1);

  % Influence coefficients (Hess & Smith style)
  eps = 1e-14;
  A = -(1/(2*pi)) * log( ((xt - L)^2 + yt^2) / max(eps, (xt^2 + yt^2)) );
  B = (atan2(yt, xt - L) - atan2(yt, xt));

  % Normal component is combination of A and B with panel orientation
  % In local frame: vn = B (since derivative of potential along tangent); map to global normal:
  % More complete form:
  vn_local = B; % normal influence in local coordinates
  % Convert local normal (positive y_local) to global using panel normal components
  aij = vn_local * 1; % already corresponds to unit normal when mapped at collocation

  % Project to global normal of panel i
  % Empirically, the local-normal value equals contribution to global-normal due to orthogonality of transforms.
  % For robustness, re-project velocity vector components:
  % Compute induced velocity vector in global frame from unit source panel j at point i
  [u,v] = velocity_from_unit_source_panel(xci,yci,x1,y1,x2,y2);
  aij = u*pi.nx + v*pi.ny;
end

function tij = panel_source_tangential_influence(pi, pj)
  % Tangential velocity at collocation of panel i due to unit-strength source panel j
  [u,v] = velocity_from_unit_source_panel(pi.xc, pi.yc, pj.x1, pj.y1, pj.x2, pj.y2);
  tij = u*pi.tx + v*pi.ty;
end

function [u,v] = velocity_from_unit_source_panel(x,y,x1,y1,x2,y2)
  % Induced velocity of a constant-strength unit source panel from (x1,y1) to (x2,y2) at field point (x,y).
  % Based on analytical integrals for 2D source segments.
  dx = x2 - x1; dy = y2 - y1; L = hypot(dx,dy);
  ct = dx/L; st = dy/L;
  % Transform point to panel local coordinates
  xp =  ct*(x - x1) + st*(y - y1);
  yp = -st*(x - x1) + ct*(y - y1);
  % Avoid singularities
  eps = 1e-14;
  x2p = L; x1p = 0;
  % Analytical expressions
  term1 = log(((x2p - xp)^2 + yp^2) / max(eps, (x1p - xp)^2 + yp^2));
  term2 = atan2(yp, x2p - xp) - atan2(yp, x1p - xp);
  % Velocity in local coordinates due to unit source strength (per unit length integrated):
  u_loc = term1/(2*pi);        % along panel tangent (x_local)
  v_loc = term2/(2*pi);        % along panel normal  (y_local)
  % Rotate back to global
  u =  ct*u_loc - st*v_loc;
  v =  st*u_loc + ct*v_loc;
end

function [Lprime, CL] = forces_from_panels(panels, rho, Uinf, Vt, gamma)
  % Pressure coefficient to pressure difference => integrate to lift per unit span.
  N = numel(panels);
  Cp = 1 - (Vt./Uinf).^2;
  % Pressure on surface: p = p_inf + 0.5*rho*Uinf^2 * Cp
  % Differential force normal to surface: -p * n * ds. Lift is vertical component.
  Lprime = 0;
  for i=1:N
    p = 0.5*rho*Uinf^2 * Cp(i);
    dFx = -p * panels(i).nx * panels(i).len;
    dFy = -p * panels(i).ny * panels(i).len;
    % Lift positive upward = dFy
    Lprime = Lprime + dFy;
  end
  % Kutta-Joukowski reference CL using circulation gamma and reference length as chord estimate
  % Here we estimate chord as max(x)-min(x)
  xs = [panels.x1 panels(end).x2]; xs = xs(:);
  c_ref = max(xs) - min(xs);
  if c_ref <= 0; c_ref = mean([panels.len]); end
  CL = Lprime / (0.5*rho*Uinf^2*c_ref);
  % Also, user may compare L' ~= rho*Uinf*gamma
  if abs(gamma) > 0
    Lprime_KJ = rho*Uinf*gamma;
    fprintf('  Kutta-Joukowski L'' (rho Uinf Gamma) = %.6g [N/m]\n', Lprime_KJ);
  end
end

function [xc,yc,R] = fit_circle(xy)
  % Simple algebraic circle fit (Kasa method)
  x = xy(:,1); y = xy(:,2);
  A = [2*x, 2*y, ones(size(x))];
  b = x.^2 + y.^2;
  sol = A\b;
  xc = sol(1); yc = sol(2);
  R = sqrt(max(0, sol(3) + xc^2 + yc^2));
end

