Below is an incremental improvement of the earlier toy translator (SQL AST -> Relational Algebra AST) with focused error handling, practical pitfalls, and concrete examples that show input SQL and the resulting RA trees (or errors). It remains Python-only and builds on the iterative path: single-table SELECT, multiple tables (implicit joins), and explicit JOIN.

Note: We still assume you start from an existing SQL AST, not raw SQL text. Small catalogs are optional but enable much better error messages and name resolution. The examples include both the human-friendly SQL string and the corresponding SelectStmt construction so you can see what the translator expects.

