Performance and visual tips
- Use requestAnimationFrame, clamp dt, and devicePixelRatio transforms to keep drawing crisp.
- Keep Canvas draw calls minimal; batch styles and avoid per‑frame heavy allocations.
- Limit orbit line alpha and widths; avoid shadow blur for many bodies.
- Provide min pixel radius for visibility; optionally color-code planets.
- Consider culling drawing for planets whose orbits exceed canvas extents.
- Debounce resize and recalc transforms only when needed.

What you should see
- A dark canvas with the Sun at center.
- Circular orbits for the 8 planets; planets revolve at relative speeds matching NASA orbital periods.
- Distances between orbits reflect scaled semimajor axes from NASA data.

Notes
- The Planetary Fact Sheet sometimes updates formatting; the scraper locates rows by label prefixes to remain resilient. Verify planets.json contents after generation.
- All data used for semimajor axis, orbital period, and radius come from the NASA Planetary Fact Sheet (Metric) link above; the JSON written includes the source URL for traceability.

